Training a Dogo Argentino requires early consistency, firm leadership, and positive reinforcemnet, as the breed is strong, intelligent, and naturally protective.

Key training principles 

Start early: Begin structured training and socialization right away at8 weeks of age before independent or stubborn behavior emerge during adolescence. 

Prioritize Socialization: Expose your puppy to many different people, animals, and environments to prevent fear-based aggresion or over-protectives. 

Use Positive Reinforcement: Reward desired behaviors using high-value treats (such as deer jerky, sweet potato, or cheese) or toys, as fear-based or harsh training methods can trigger resistance and defensive.

Establish Clear boundaries: Be calm, consistent leader. Dogos form deep bonds with their handlers andd need clear rules to prevent dominances issues.
